Z||000025||StuGood||11-20-2000||12:52 PM||||"If you didn't have a Fiero..." <BR>Time to 'fess up.  I <B>don't</B> own a Fiero.  That's right  I don't have a <B>single</B> Fiero to my name.  I feel so ashamed....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Reason: Because I have <B>four</B> Fieros!  <B>Four</B> Fieros to my name   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !<P>"If you didn't have a Fiero..." Kind of a depressing thought!  I'd probably have a Chevy Cavalier like the one I own now, 3.1 w/5-speed.  And I'd be busy using parts from it, to build a kit car that looked like...<BR>A Fiero   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !! <P>If it had to be an "off the shelf" car, I guess a 2nd generation MR2.  Definitely <B>not</B> a Fiat X-one-ninth! <BR>-------------------------------------------<BR>BTW, 286SE'S, my (bad) impression of X-1/9's is based on my experiences with (working on, and driving) just 2 of them.  But never owning one...  so maybe those 2 were not representative.  Unfortunately, first impressions tend to be lasting, and that's why I said I would't have one.  No offense intended  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!  Glad you still like yours  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 11-20-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000026||286SE'S||11-20-2000||01:24 PM||||No reason to bash the Fiat X1/9 it was a nice car (at least mine was) I put 40,000 miles on mine before the engine died at 112,000. Since the car came from the east it was so rusty I decided not to waste any money on repairs. If I had not gotten a Fiero I would have bought another X1/9, I actually looked at one the day before I got the Fiero but it was black with red interior and I didn't care for that at all. The Fiat has a weight advantage that it weighs about 800 lbs less than a Fiero and the handling is much better, it was also very quiet. The 2M4 engine is very rattly. I don't miss my X1/9 as it is sitting in my yard slowly sinking into the mud. I can appreciate its beauty but not its performance or problems. I can take the targa top off on a nice day and play the radio. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
