Z||000029||Smokey||11-20-2000||02:04 PM||||If there was never a fiero, I wouldn't have lost all that money on my old one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I don't own a fiero anymore. I was stupid and traded it for an Rx-7. I miss it really bad! truly beautiful car. But I just couldn't keep her running as much as I liked. So I went for the Rx-7. Kept the "2 seater" style w/ more room, more space for a system, little more get up and go, and a 5 speed to boot. I thought about going and buying my fiero back...but I have 78 grand prix to go along with the rx-7. 3 cars to fix when they break is a little more than I'd like to put up with  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> And the grand prix is under "hot rod" construction right now, so I really don't have to money for another toy.  Maybe one day I'll have another plastic rocket. Untill then...you'll know I'm comming when u smell rice cookin!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and Imports STILL suck! ||||reg||6
