Z||000035||MikeE||11-20-2000||07:48 PM||||I used to have a Porche 914 and I liked it but they became too expensive to consider as a project car.  I also had a 260Z but they are rust buckets.<P>I saw the Fiero as a better looking alternative with more potential for mods.  Here in Hawaii, however, the resistance to rust is very important.  To me, it's just not worth sinking money into a car that is going to rust out before long (all the nice cars here do).  It's an ongoing problem that keeps the bodymen happy.  That doesn't leave many alternatives (in a rust-free material) that I like.  I can't afford a Corvette, or the insurance, and I don't like the new ones anyway.  Saturns don't do anything for me either.<P>Based on that, I would probably get one of GM's plastic vans (Lumina APV, Transport, Silloette) and turn it into my version of the ultimate hot rod surf van (90's style, not 70's).  In fact, I may still do that.  However, would that van exist if not for the Fiero?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000036||bHooper||11-20-2000||10:52 PM||||no fiero.. hmmm.<P>i gave up my CRX for a my GT in '89.<BR>and have since it broke (though now it runs), i have owned a '91 RX-7 (dog) and a '98 Cherokee (current daily driver).<P>though the years, there were times that i came close to trading my GT.  i looked at the '93 RX-7 (nice!), the Corado,a Prelude, 2nd G Mr-2... oh, and when we had the recall back in '90, i damn near traded the thing in on a dodge daytona (yuk!!!)! i talked to a salesman several times, but never ever pulled the trigger.  (although i came very close on that Rx-7!)<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/alien.gif">   <BR>We are not alone!||||reg||1
Z||000037||William||11-20-2000||11:02 PM||||Fiat x-1/9<BR>ferarri 308 (if I could find the money)<P>I've always beleived that the fiero was a visual blend of these 2 cars. I fell in love with the x-1/9 when I had test driven 2 that were at a local lot when I turned sixteen. Dad was helping out with the wheels and said NO WAY!! :-( I never did own one but always wanted to get one through the years that followed. The x-1/9 is a big big reason why I love the fiero and in some ways I like the looks of the car even more than the fiero. The only thing that always held be back was the storys of rust and reliability. Anyone remember the truimph TR-7? I liked that one too, even though the engine was placed in the wrong position. Buy the way, I spotted a ferarri 308 / fiero kit car this weekend and was pleased to see how simular it was to my 85 se coupe!||||reg||1
